{"id":"standing_cable_adduction","name":"Standing cable adduction","cue":"Stand tall and sweep the leg across in front of the other.","research":"Standing cable hip adduction, right leg working, the column on the right. Design values from the standard technique description, not a measured trial: standing tall on the left leg (knee 3, the sole flat on the plate), the right hand on a vertical grab bar of the column (0.32 H out), the left hand at the hip, the trunk leaning 4 deg toward the standing side and the pelvis kept level. A cuff on the right ankle carries a ring on its outer side, and the cable runs from the low pulley (0.075 H, beside the column) straight out to it, so it pulls the ankle out toward the column and the leg is swept inward against it. The stretch is the leg held out toward the column (24 deg of hip abduction, the foot 0.24 H out and 0.1 H up, hip flexion 7, knee 6); the finish is the leg across the midline in front of the standing leg (14 deg of hip adduction, rig limit 25, hip flexion 25, knee 7, the ankle 0.16 H ahead and 0.1 H up), so the foot passes above and in front of the standing foot with about 3 cm to spare. Cable 1:1 to the stack. Geometry: design/cable/ad.mjs.","targets":{"tol":10,"A":{"hip_abduction_r":24,"hip_flexion_r":7,"knee_flexion_r":6,"knee_flexion_l":3},"B":{"hip_abduction_r":-14,"hip_flexion_r":25,"knee_flexion_r":7},"note":"design values (standard technique), not a measured trial"},"muscles":{"primary":["adductors"],"secondary":[],"side":"r"},"camera":{"az":325,"el":15,"dAz":0,"dEl":0,"fill":0.6,"note":"From the front and to the left of the lifter (az 325 = 35 deg left of the front, el 15): the inner thigh of the right leg faces the camera as the leg sweeps in, and the standing leg stays behind it so the crossing in front reads. The column is on the far side with its grab bar and cable."},"rhythm":false,"motion":{"mirror":false,"tempo":[1,0.5,2.5,0.5],"root":[-0.05,0.53,0],"base":{"pelvis":{"flex":0,"lat":0},"lumbar":{"flex